## Supervisor fix: the spike is reachable without the cable (in scope: the spike gates G16H)
Defect (source, MEASURED by reading measurement_main.cpp): BLESPIKE was a USB-console verb only; a TUNE session
aborts a running spike (spike_service "tune"); the ota.auto_s=120 self-fetch poll joins the owner network every
120 s and would take the radio in the middle of a 60 s phase. The stick's USB is only its charger (opening it resets).
Fix:
- adapters/tune/session.cpp allowed() + tools/tune_session.py: BLESPIKE, BLESPIKE start [<1-3 digits> <1 digit>],
  BLESPIKE stop/report/phases accepted over Wi-Fi.
  RED  builds/20261119-g16h-spike-wifi/red-tune_session_check.log (7 of 7 new assertions failed),
       red-test_tune_session.log (1 failed).
  GREEN green-tune_session_check.log (73 assertions), green-asan-tune_session_check.log (ASan+UBSan), green-test_tune_session.log (7 passed).
- measurement_main.cpp (spike image only): over Wi-Fi `BLESPIKE start` ARMS the run; spike_arm_service() starts it
  after the session, once the Guardian monitors the selected AP (gives up after 180 s); self-fetch poll and
  dim/sleep wait while armed or running; BLESPIKE phases prints every phase line; start errors land in last_end.
